<section class="fcd-section" id="startup">
    <h2>What happens when the website starts</h2>
    <p>From <code>Program.cs</code>, in order:</p>
    <ol>
        <li>Loads <code>appsettings.json</code> (plus <code>appsettings.{Environment}.json</code> outside Production) and environment variables.</li>
        <li>Registers sessions (30-minute idle timeout, Secure cookie), localisation (7 languages, default <code>en-GB</code> formatting with English text), Razor Pages and controllers.</li>
        <li>Connects to Azure Key Vault (<code>KEY_VAULT_URL</code> in Production, <code>Keyvault:Url</code> otherwise) using <code>EnvironmentCredential</code>, and adds the vault as a configuration source.</li>
        <li>Chooses the database connection string: <code>ConnectionStrings:Development</code> in Development, the <code>db-connection-live</code> secret in Production.</li>
        <li>Configures Serilog (Loki + MariaDB), EF Core with MySQL, Identity, permission policies and the password policy.</li>
        <li>Sets Identity token lifetime to 2 hours and configures the anti-forgery cookie/header names.</li>
        <li>Configures ASP.NET Data Protection: keys in Blob Storage, wrapped with a Key Vault key in Production; a local <code>DataProtectionKeys</code> folder in Development. See <a href="/docs/system/data#encryption">encryption</a>.</li>
        <li>Configures cookies, CORS, HSTS, Elmah, Hangfire (MySQL storage, up to 20 workers), application services, SignalR and the image-migration hosted service.</li>
        <li>Ensures the Blob container exists and registers the blob URL and upload services.</li>
        <li>Reads the JWT settings and, if ChurchSuite OAuth settings are present, registers the <code>ChurchSuite</code> OAuth scheme; always registers JWT bearer authentication.</li>
        <li>Builds the request pipeline (next section), maps Razor Pages, controllers and <code>/logsHub</code>.</li>
        <li>Applies any pending EF Core migrations, then runs the seeder: ensures the <code>bulletins</code> table and columns, adds missing permissions, creates the three built-in roles if missing, and creates the SuperAdmin account if missing.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>If anything throws during start-up, the exception is written to <code>logs/Error-yyyyMMdd.log</code> and the <code>logs</code> folder is zipped to <code>support/SupportData-yyyyMd.zip</code>, then the process exits.</p>
</section>

<section class="fcd-section" id="pipeline">
    <h2>The request pipeline</h2>
    <p>Each request passes through these steps in this order:</p>
    <div class="fcd-table-wrap">
        <table class="fcd-table">
            <thead><tr><th>#</th><th>Step</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr><td>1</td><td>Exception handler + HSTS</td><td>Outside Development only: errors go to <code>/Error</code>; HSTS header sent.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>2</td><td>Header clean-up</td><td>Removes <code>Server</code> and <code>X-Powered-By</code>; adds <code>Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains; preload</code>.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>3</td><td>HTTPS redirection</td><td>Redirects HTTP to HTTPS.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>4</td><td>Serilog request logging</td><td>One log line per request.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>5</td><td>Static files</td><td>Serves <code>wwwroot</code> (registered twice; harmless).</td></tr>
                <tr><td>6</td><td>Routing, culture cookie</td><td><code>?culture=xx</code> sets the culture cookie for a month.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>7</td><td>Request localisation, session</td><td>Query string → cookie → browser language.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>8</td><td>Authentication, authorisation, Elmah</td><td>Cookie sign-in (Identity), optional ChurchSuite OAuth, JWT bearer.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>9</td><td>File-type filter</td><td>Blocks requests for paths with a dot unless the extension is in an allow-list (css, js, images, fonts). Runs after static files, so it only affects paths that weren't served as files.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>10</td><td>Anti-forgery</td><td>Validates the CSRF token on every POST/PUT/DELETE except Login, Register, Logout, ExternalLogin, <code>/api/*</code> and <code>/dist/*</code>.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>11</td><td>Hangfire dashboard</td><td><code>/hangfire</code>, HTTP Basic auth.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>12</td><td>Endpoints</td><td>Razor Pages, MVC controllers, <code>/logsHub</code>.</td></tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </div>
</section>

