                <tr><td><code>Areas/Identity/</code></td><td>Sign-in, registration, password reset and the church-admin account pages (<code>Account/Manage</code>); <code>Data/ForestChurchesContext.cs</code> is the EF Core context.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>Areas/Admin/Pages/Bulletin</code></td><td>Bulletin admin.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>Components/</code></td><td>Services: Configuration (Key Vault, seeding, policies), Email, EventManagement, Http (Google, ChurchSuite), Logging, Permissions, Roles, Security (encoder, JWT, CSP), Storage (Blob), UserRegistration (whitelist), Ui (text helpers).</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>Controllers/</code></td><td><code>/health</code>, <code>/api/Bulletin</code>, ChurchSuite OAuth controllers; <code>/api/SystemStats</code> lives in <code>Components/Performance</code>.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>Models/</code>, <code>Migrations/</code></td><td>Entities and EF Core migrations.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>templates/</code></td><td>Copies of the email templates (the email app uses its own copies).</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>SharedResources.*.resx</code></td><td>UI text in en, cs, de, fa, fr, th, uk.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>wwwroot/css/forest.css</code>, <code>wwwroot/js/forest.js</code></td><td>The Forest Floor design system.</td></tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="fcd-section" id="hosting">
    <h2>Hosting and deployment</h2>
    <h3>Website</h3>
    <ul>
        <li><code>Dockerfile</code>: multi-stage .NET 8 build; the runtime image listens on port <strong>8080</strong> over HTTP. TLS is expected to be terminated in front of it.</li>
        <li><code>.github/workflows/deploy.yml</code>: on a push to the <code>live</code> branch, runs <code>dotnet test</code>, builds and pushes <code>ghcr.io/&lt;owner&gt;/forest_churches:live</code>, signs in to Azure and deploys to the Azure Container App <code>forestchurches</code> in resource group <code>myResourceGroup</code>.</li>
        <li>Required environment variables in production: <code>ASPNETCORE_ENVIRONMENT=Production</code>, <code>KEY_VAULT_URL</code>, <code>AZURE_TENANT_ID</code>, <code>AZURE_CLIENT_ID</code>, <code>AZURE_CLIENT_SECRET</code>. Optional: <code>CHURCHSUITE_OAUTH_*</code>. See <a href="/docs/system/configuration">Configuration</a>.</li>
        <li><code>docker-compose.yml</code> is a local-development helper that builds both apps side by side.</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>Email app</h3>
    <ul>
        <li>Its own <code>Dockerfile</code> (ports 8080/8081). The recent commits target a Plesk server (Passenger), and start-up errors are written to the console so Plesk shows them.</li>
        <li>Needs the same Key Vault variables: <code>KEY_VAULT_URL</code>, <code>AZURE_TENANT_ID</code>, <code>AZURE_CLIENT_ID</code>, <code>AZURE_CLIENT_SECRET</code>. Templates are copied into the publish output.</li>
        <li><code>EnableSwaggerInProduction</code> is <code>true</code> in <code>appsettings.json</code>, so <code>/swagger</code> is public in production.</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>Database</h3>
    <p>MySQL 8 / MariaDB, reached through the connection string in <code>db-connection-live</code>. EF Core applies migrations automatically at start-up. Hangfire creates its own <code>Hangfire*</code> tables in the same database, and Serilog creates <code>applicationlogs</code>.</p>
</section>
